From: jiro28 <ktgithub28@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 21:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] config: preloaded-classes: Preload android.util.StatsLog

Some hardened apps (e.g. banking RASP wrappers) load a native library
from a class initializer whose JNI_OnLoad opens a TLS connection. When
another thread is already inside a System.loadLibrary() holding the
Runtime lock, Conscrypt's handshake path reaches
ConscryptStatsLog.write -> android.util.StatsLog.<clinit>, which calls
System.loadLibrary("stats_jni") and blocks on that same Runtime lock.
The two threads deadlock and the app ANRs at startup ("failed to
complete startup").

Preloading android.util.StatsLog in zygote runs its class initializer
(and loads stats_jni) once, before any fork, so the app never triggers
the lazy <clinit> on a locked path. Fixes the TPBank (com.tpb.mb.
gprsandroid) startup hang.

Change-Id: I5ta7510900000000000000000000000000000000
---
 config/preloaded-classes | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/config/preloaded-classes
+++ b/config/preloaded-classes
@@ -9054,6 +9054,7 @@
 android.util.Spline$MonotoneCubicSpline
 android.util.Spline
 android.util.StateSet
+android.util.StatsLog
 android.util.StringBuilderPrinter
 android.util.SuperNotCalledException
 android.util.SystemConfigFileCommitEventLogger
